-- title:
--   The prescribed sample count covers the finite-family estimation budget
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, $I=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, $E=I\times\{0,1\}$, and $\Omega=\mathcal P(E)$. Let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean oracles on subsets of $I$. Write $R(S)$ for the natural-number value of the paired-rank routine with parameter $r$ and these oracles, and $d(S)=n-R(S)$ with subtraction truncated at zero. Let $p=(\varepsilon,\delta)$ consist of rational parameters $0<\varepsilon,\delta<1$. Write $s=\operatorname{setup}(n,p)$ for the prescribed annealing schedule, $L=s.L$ for its phase count, $\rho=s.\rho$ for its temperature ratio, $\eta=s.\eta$ for its relative mean tolerance, and $N=s.\mathrm{observations}$ for its sample count. Assume $n>0$ and let $|\mathcal O|=n^2+2$ be the number of observable indices, including the repeated diagonal indicators. Then $$\eta>0,\quad N>0,\quad \frac{(n^2+2)(40000n^8/N)}{(\eta/(20n^2))^2}\le\frac1{32(L+1)}.$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/FinitePhaseEstimationBound.lean#L13-L65

